<VI _name="Unit-Test.lvlib:velocity-rms-kurtosis-test.vi" description="PURPOSE\0AUnit test for the two channels added to PowerSpectrum.vi (Calculations.lvlib)\3A Velocity RMS and Kurtosis. Checks the g-&gt;m/s2 scaling\2C the SVL Integration setup (single integration\2C mm\2C 10 Hz highpass) and the Build Array order.\0A\0AHOW IT WORKS\0A1. Synthesises a continuous-phase sine (Amplitude g pk at Frequency Hz\2C fs = Sample Rate) and cuts it into blocks of Samples per Block\2C like FlexLogger feeds Process.vi.\0A2. Calls PowerSpectrum.vi once per block from ONE call site\2C so the integration filter state carries over between blocks as in the plugin. Early blocks show the highpass start-up transient.\0A3. Reads the LAST TWO waveforms of Array of Waveforms\3A second-to-last = Kurtosis (Kurt)\2C last = Velocity RMS (VelRMS). Matches the Initialize.vi name lists\3A PBand\2C Crest\2C Peak\2C RMS\2C Max\2C Min\2C Max-Min\2C Skew\2C Kurt\2C VelRMS.\0A4. Compares the final block with the theory.\0A\0AEXPECTED (pure sine)\0AVelocity RMS [mm/s] = A x 9806.65 / (2 pi f) / sqrt(2). Default 1 g pk at 159.15 Hz = 6.94 mm/s.\0AKurtosis = 1.5 (sine). Gaussian noise = 3. Impacts &gt; 3.\0A\0AHOW TO USE\0ARun with the defaults. PASS = both checks true.\0A- Velocity 1000x low\3A the g-&gt;mm/s2 multiply is 9.80665 instead of 9806.65 (SVL Integration with length units = mm expects mm/s2 in).\0A- Values swapped\3A Build Array order wrong.\0A- Kurtosis about -1.5\3A the VI reports excess kurtosis.\0AVelocity RMS per Block shows the filter settling. Parameter Count must be 10 (the number of names in Initialize.vi).">
